        "original_id": "ea8d598e-8b64-555e-8cd4-e04c135ac540",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Huell Howser\n- Works: California's Gold, Winnie the Pooh (2011), Malibu Public Beach Safari\n- Organizations: KCET, California PBS stations, LA Urban Rangers, Disney\n\nFacts:\n- Huell Howser was born on October 18, 1945, and died on January 7, 2013.\n- Huell Howser was an American television personality, actor, producer, writer, singer, and voice artist.\n- Huell Howser was best known for hosting, producing, and writing California's Gold.\n- KCET in Los Angeles produced California's Gold for California PBS stations.\n- Winnie the Pooh was released in 2011 and was Disney's 51st animated feature film.\n- Huell Howser voiced the Backson in Winnie the Pooh (2011).\n- The LA Urban Rangers' longest-running and most recent outing was the Malibu Public Beach Safari.\n- Huell Howser featured the Malibu Public Beach Safari on his show, and media reports also covered it.",
